# Rule - Definition of Done

Open process files through `{workspace}/artifacts-map.json`. Join `{workspace}` and each stored path. Do not prefix `artifacts_root` again.

A check names a result a person can confirm. A file on disk, a green local run, or a link alone is not that result.

Apply defaults for the work type, then checks on the process artifact. A replacement checklist on an artifact replaces defaults for that scope only. An additional check adds to defaults.

Write order when more than one process file changes: `changes-log.md`, `issues-log.md`, `status.md` (draft, user confirm, then write), `sprint-backlog.md`, `product-backlog.md`. Skip a file when it does not apply.

## When to update status.md

Update `status.md` when closing a PBI, SBI, OGT, or sprint under the sections below, or when the user explicitly asks for a status refresh. Do not update `status.md` after every internal task while an SBI stays WIP. WIP checkpoints while an item is not Done follow [`sdd-realtime-status.mdc`](./sdd-realtime-status.mdc).

When writing `status.md`, follow the section and OGT rules in `{client_root}/templates/framework.sdd.works/sdd-scrum-practices.md` `#statusmd`.

## Common quality gate

A deliverable is a software feature or another shipped result, such as a document, a rule, a skill, or a seed.

This gate applies to a PBI, an SBI, and a RID. It does not apply to an OGT. A sprint does not add a second pass.

The checks below are the common list. Extra quality checks named for this deliverable are part of this gate. Examples are `test-strategy.md` and `{stem}-tests.md`. Other named files count too. A named file may be on `{workspace}/artifacts-map.json` or a spec outside that map. Open the file at the path the artifact names.

- [ ] The deliverable matches the stated outcome.
- [ ] A person can confirm the result. A file on disk or a green local run alone does not pass.
- [ ] The verification for this deliverable was used: an automated test, a review, or the method the artifact names.
- [ ] A failure or empty case was checked when this deliverable has one.
- [ ] Extra quality checks named for this deliverable passed. `test-strategy.md` and `{stem}-tests.md` are examples, not the full list.
- [ ] The deliverable contains no secrets.

Skip a box that does not apply and state why in one sentence.

## Close confirm

**Artifact confirm** is the user reply that lets the agent write engineering or pack files. It is not **close confirm**.

**Close confirm** is the user reply that accepts the backlog item for close. It must appear in chat before any `**Done**` row on `sprint-backlog.md` or `product-backlog.md`, before sprint **Status: Done**, before RID move to Closed RIDs, and before `status.md` shows that item as **Done**.

Close confirm counts when the user explicitly accepts the deliverable (names the SBI or PBI code, says **Done** for that row, or answers yes to the close question). It does not count when the user only asked to implement a plan, finish todos, or ship files without accepting close.

Before close confirm, run **sdd-retrospective** when the defaults require it. After close confirm, write process files in the order under **Write order** above.

Ask once in chat, then wait for the next user message:

Do you confirm {scope} is usable for your work?

Replace `{scope}` with the SBI name, PBI noun, sprint goal, or RID id from the backlog row. For a document, seed, rule, or skill, **usable** means acceptable to rely on, not only runnable in a browser.

When **persistent-proactive-developer** or plan completion would write **Done**, **sdd-dod.mdc** wins for backlog close writes.

## PBI

Defaults: acceptance criteria passed; Common quality gate passed; user confirmed usable; `sdd-retrospective` skill completed or nothing durable to persist.

Extra: Additional DoD criteria in the Definition of Done section of `product-backlog.md` (after Product overview; standard defaults remain in this rule).

Write the `product-backlog.md` row `Done` only after `sdd-retrospective` finishes in the same session.

After confirm: `changes-log.md` when a change concludes; `issues-log.md` when a linked defect closes; `status.md`; `sprint-backlog.md` when Unplanned PBIs or parent text must match; `product-backlog.md` row `Done`.

## SBI

Defaults: acceptance criteria passed; Common quality gate passed; user confirmed usable; `sdd-retrospective` skill completed or nothing durable to persist.

Extra: `sprint-backlog.md` DoD section links to Definition of Done in `product-backlog.md`; sprint replacement above its tables; Additional Done Criteria on the row.

An SBI may be `Done` while its parent PBI stays `ToDo` or `WIP`.

Write the `sprint-backlog.md` row `Done` only after `sdd-retrospective` finishes in the same session.

After confirm: `changes-log.md` when a change concludes; `issues-log.md` when a linked defect closes; `status.md`; `sprint-backlog.md` row `Done`; `product-backlog.md` when the PBI checklist is fully satisfied.

## RID

A RID (risk, impediment, dependency) is recorded only in the RID Log on `sprint-backlog.md`. It is not a PBI, SBI, or OGT.

Defaults: solution verified with a confirmable result; Common quality gate passed; user confirmed close; `sdd-retrospective` skill when a durable lesson exists, otherwise state that explicitly.

After confirm: `changes-log.md` when closure concludes a change; `sprint-backlog.md` moves the row from Open RIDs to Closed RIDs with Closed Sprint.

## OGT

Defaults: outcome stated and user confirmed; `sdd-retrospective` skill when a durable lesson exists, otherwise state that explicitly.

An OGT is not a PBI and not an SBI.

After confirm: `changes-log.md` when a change concludes; `status.md` moves the row from open OGT to closed OGT.

## Sprint

Defaults: every SBI in the sprint is `Done`; sprint goal true and user confirmed the sprint; Retrospective under that sprint or `sdd-retrospective` skill at sprint-end.

After confirm: `changes-log.md` for sprint close; `issues-log.md` when sprint work closes a defect; `status.md`; `sprint-backlog.md` sprint **Status: Done**; `product-backlog.md` for PBIs finished in the sprint.

## Do not

- Close or mark `Done` without the user confirmations the defaults require.
- Mark an SBI or PBI **Done** in the same turn as the last deliverable edit without **close confirm** in a prior or same-thread user message.
- Treat artifact confirm, plan completion, or internal todo completion as **close confirm**.
- Weaken or skip a check to reach `Done` or RID close.
- Show `Done` on `status.md` for a PBI, SBI, or sprint that the backlog does not show as `Done`.
- Invent a sprint, SBI, or OGT row on `status.md`.
- Write `status.md` without the user's confirmation.
